Save and close.

3. Confirm what git will track now

cmd
git status

You should see only .gitignore and index.html (plus maybe node_modules/ line, harmless).

4. Commit and push

cmd
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit - latest invoice tracker as index.html"
git push -u origin main

Once pushed, go set up Netlify (Part 2 from earlier) pointing at this repo, publish directory . — it'll auto-serve index.html.

One flag: that file's ~2.5MB, which is large for a single HTML file (likely embedded data/images/base64). That's fine for git and Netlify, just slower to load in browser — not something to fix now, just worth knowing.